  "goodToKnow": "Das Wappen is a coat of arms: das Stadtwappen, das Familienwappen. Germany's federal Wappen shows the black Bundesadler (eagle) on gold, and Berlin's shows a bear, Munich's a monk (the Münchner Kindl). Das Wappentier is the heraldic animal. Wappen comes from a Low German form of Waffe (weapon), because coats of arms were painted on shields to recognise knights in armour. The plural is the same."
